    "report_markdown": "# Hypora run report: run_229e9b484787\n\n**Outcome:** a verified model.\n\n## Task\n- Objective: Identify which website sessions will end in a purchase so the marketing team can act on them.\n- Target: `Revenue` (binary_classification)\n- Primary metric: `roc_auc` (maximize)\n\n## Summary\nThe run aimed to identify website sessions likely to end in a purchase, so the marketing team can act on them. Several candidate models and a logistic regression baseline were evaluated, and a verified ExtraTrees model was delivered. Its test ROC AUC was 0.9315.\n\n**Observations**\n- The selected model achieved validation ROC AUC of 0.9251.\n- On the test split, precision was 0.5714 and recall was 0.7273.\n- The model passed the reported verification checks, and its frozen artifact loaded and made test-split predictions.\n\n**Limitations**\n- A leakage candidate was flagged and requires methodological review; this run does not establish that leakage is absent.\n- The learned-transform leakage check was skipped, so this aspect was not verified.\n- Test metrics describe this split and do not establish performance in future sessions or other settings.\n\n_Written by the Reporter; every number above is filled in from stored metrics._\n\n## Final model\n- Trial `trl_4867b5e4`: An ExtraTrees ensemble will capture complex interactions in the behavioral metrics and provide a strong ranker with reduced variance across diverse randomized trees.\n- Verified: yes\n\n| Metric | Test (once) | Validation (mean) |\n|---|---|---|\n| roc_auc | 0.9315 | 0.9251 |\n| accuracy | 0.8735 | 0.8851 |\n| balanced_accuracy | 0.8138 | 0.8225 |\n| precision | 0.5714 | 0.6072 |\n| recall | 0.7273 | 0.7319 |\n| f1 | 0.6400 | 0.6635 |\n| precision_macro | 0.7595 | 0.7781 |\n| recall_macro | 0.8138 | 0.8225 |\n| f1_macro | 0.7816 | 0.7971 |\n| pr_auc | 0.7506 | 0.7244 |\n| log_loss | 0.2474 | 0.2603 |\n| brier_score | 0.0800 | 0.0809 |\n\n| Check | Status | Detail |\n|---|---|---|\n| allowed_features | passed | trial code received exactly the contract's allowed features |\n| split_respected | passed | stratified split: disjoint, complete |\n| test_labels_not_accessed | passed | every predict stage saw features and the model only |\n| output_shape | passed | one prediction per planned row, task-shaped columns |\n| finite_outputs | passed | all predictions finite and well-formed |\n| metric_recomputation | passed | recomputed metrics match the harness |\n| artifact_loads | passed | the frozen model loaded in a sandbox and predicted the test split |\n| resource_limits | passed | every stage completed inside the submitted job's limits |\n| learned_transform_leakage | skipped | static analysis of fit/predict arrives with verifier v2 (S3.C4) |\n\n## Trials\n| Trial | Kind | Status | Validation roc_auc (mean \u00b1 std, folds) | Hypothesis |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `trl_4867b5e4` | candidate | verified | 0.9251 \u00b1 0.0032 (3) | An ExtraTrees ensemble will capture complex interactions in the behavioral metrics and provide a strong ranker with reduced variance across diverse randomized trees. |\n| `trl_c0ce2069` | candidate | validated | 0.9207 \u00b1 0.0041 (3) | A moderately deeper, more slowly trained histogram booster with larger leaves may better capture feature interactions without overfitting this modest, imbalanced dataset. |\n| `trl_cc649788` | candidate | validated | 0.9250 \u00b1 0.0045 (3) | A regularized histogram gradient booster can capture nonlinear thresholds and interactions in session behavior while retaining the PageValues signal. |\n| `trl_f3b60256` | baseline | validated | 0.8889 \u00b1 0.0033 (3) | A standardized logistic regression establishes a regularized linear probability-ranking baseline using all approved features. |\n\n## Data\n- Split: stratified, 20% test, stratified_kfold_3\n- Features used: 17; excluded: none\n- Leakage screen: Leakage candidates flagged: 1 among 17 screened features; methodological review is required.\n\n## Decision and faults\n- Decision: train (approved_plan)\n\n## Run notes\n- Stage-1 placeholder (D-019): contract built by code, plan approved by policy; replaced by the Data Lead (S3.A2) and the plan gate (S3.D2).\n- The agent finished after 16 model turns, 21 tool calls; it nominated trl_4867b5e4.\n- Final candidate trl_4867b5e4: nominated by the agent.\n- Final job job_1794151283029073158_c31f82: test split scored once; verifier v1 passed.\n\n## Sources\n- `task_spec:run_229e9b484787.v1`\n- `profile:run_229e9b484787.profile.1b5f5d61e2e2`\n- `experiment_contract:run_229e9b484787.v1`\n- `result:trl_4867b5e4/test`\n"
